		},
		{
			"id": 1738284,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://seocommunity.social/@simoncox/111408420521196449",
			"author": {
				"name": "Simon Cox :SEO:",
				"url": "https://seocommunity.social/@simoncox",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/262987ea3a44345cb221531f5d20fc5b39871a78db811fc5ac990a130fde5c7a.gif"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-14T10:26:28.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Well I sorted my single Axe issue out,  had two aside tags (tut Simon), have you done yours yet?</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1909845,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com/post/3lolq6gz6sl24",
			"author": {
				"name": "Barry Pollard",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/39e4c7d9b74dac3df01f5fc54d5feaf7f1713c91569f59346464a26f1e8929ff.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-07T15:39:10.000Z",
			"content": "I mean there&apos;s already an element of comparison even in field metrics, and the limits (e.g. 2.5 secs for LCP) may not be the right limits for your site (every site is different!), but at least it&apos;s based on YOUR users. Which I argue is more important than this being a like-for-like comparison tool.",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1909844,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com/post/3lolq6gz5td24",
			"author": {
				"name": "Barry Pollard",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/39e4c7d9b74dac3df01f5fc54d5feaf7f1713c91569f59346464a26f1e8929ff.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-07T15:39:10.000Z",
			"content": "And it comes back to whether you&apos;re wanting to use metrics to measure your site&apos;s user experience? Or to compare against possibly unrelated site types?",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1909843,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com/post/3lolq6gz4u324",
			"author": {
				"name": "Barry Pollard",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/39e4c7d9b74dac3df01f5fc54d5feaf7f1713c91569f59346464a26f1e8929ff.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-07T15:39:10.000Z",
			"content": "Ideally you&apos;d test every page and ever interaction on every page, and then weigh them compared to how they&apos;re actually used in real life but that&apos;s impossible and so it&apos;s easier just to ACTUALLY measure them in real life!",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1909842,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com/post/3lolq6gllb324",
			"author": {
				"name": "Barry Pollard",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/tunetheweb.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/39e4c7d9b74dac3df01f5fc54d5feaf7f1713c91569f59346464a26f1e8929ff.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-07T15:39:10.000Z",
			"content": "It&apos;s impossible for a tool to ever fully simulate a site&apos;s actual usage cause users are weird (and wonderful!) and use a site in oh so many ways, and from so many different conditions (device, network, how many other tabs are open, extensions...etc.)",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1909846,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lolqt63ads2p",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/b3eb2c3c1566218a1527eac7f6b9398b50c4c299594467477d6b335b94fdcba1.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-07T15:50:45.000Z",
			"content": "To be clear I’m not arguing against field data, I’m arguing in favor of it being one piece of the story alongside lab data. AND I agree that we need better lab data!",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
